    "bottomLine": "The pick when 3,150 propane watts feel tight: more power on propane, long half-load run time and CO shutoff.",
    "description": "The iQ5200DF is the pick when the Champion's 3,150 propane watts feel tight. Generac rates it at 3,900 running and 5,200 starting watts on gasoline and 3,500 running and 4,700 starting on propane, from a 223cc engine with push-button electric start and a pull-cord backup. Run time is its strongest spec: Generac lists 11 hours at half load and 20 hours at a quarter load on a 20 lb cylinder, and 9 and 15 hours on the 3.2-gallon gasoline tank. COsense shuts the engine down if carbon monoxide builds up, and the panel carries two GFCI 5-20R outlets, a 120V 30-amp L5-30R locking outlet and USB-A and USB-C ports. It is parallel ready with Generac's kit #7668. Two caveats: Generac publishes no dBA figure, and its own sources list the weight as 111 lb on the product page and 107 lb on the spec sheet. One owner review on Lowe's describes a unit that would not run on propane, which Generac replaced, so run any new generator on propane once at home rather than for the first time in an outage."
