    ],
    "cons": [
      "1.53-gallon gas tank, 5 hours at half load",
      "WEN's manual lists no noise rating",
      "Labor is covered for one year only"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A light, propane-frugal RV and camping generator for people who want a 30-amp outlet without a 100 lb machine.",
    "description": "The DF360iX puts a TT-30R RV outlet on a generator light enough for one person to lift. WEN's manual rates it at 2,900 running and 3,600 surge watts on gasoline and 2,600 running and 3,500 surge on propane, from a 149cc engine, at 49.6 lb. On propane it is frugal: WEN lists 14 hours at half load on a 20 lb cylinder. On gasoline it is not, with a 1.53-gallon tank good for 5 hours at half load, so this is a generator that wants to live on propane. CO Watchdog shuts the engine down if carbon monoxide builds up, and the panel has a 5-20R duplex, the TT-30R, a 12V outlet and USB. It is parallel capable with WEN's kit. Two things to know: WEN's manual publishes no noise rating, and the home-use warranty covers parts for three years but labor for one. For an RV with a 13,500 BTU air conditioner, assume you need a soft starter at this size."
  }
];

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 1,
          name: "Home",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 2,
          name: "Best Lists",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/best-of/",
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Best Dual Fuel Inverter Generator",
          item: "https://www.allmetalbrake.com/best-dual-fuel-inverter-generator/",
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the best dual fuel inverter generator?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most homes and RVs, the Champion 4500-Watt Electric Start Dual Fuel Inverter (201319): 3,150 running watts on propane, 61 dBA at 23 feet, CO Shield and a TT-30R outlet at 99.2 lb. If you need 240V for a transfer switch, the Champion 201417 and the Westinghouse iGen12000TFc are both rated at 8,100 running watts on propane."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much power does an inverter generator lose on propane?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "About 10 percent of running watts for every model on this list. The Champion 201319 goes from 3,500 to 3,150 running watts, the Generac iQ5200DF and Westinghouse iGen5000DF from 3,900 to 3,500, and the 240V units from 9,000 to 8,100. Champion keeps starting watts equal on both fuels; Generac lowers them on propane too."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long will a dual fuel inverter run on a 20 lb propane tank?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on size and load. At a quarter load, Westinghouse lists 22 hours for the iGen5000DF, Champion 21 hours for the 201319 and Generac 20 hours for the iQ5200DF. The big 240V units manage 8 to 9 hours at a quarter load. At half load, Generac lists 11 hours for the iQ5200DF and Westinghouse 5 hours for the iGen12000TFc."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Honda make a dual fuel inverter generator?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not as a factory model in the U.S. Honda's inverter generators, including the EU2200i and EU3200i, run on gasoline. Propane-capable Hondas for sale are aftermarket conversions or kits, which can affect warranty coverage. For factory propane with a full maker's warranty, choose a brand on this list."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a dual fuel inverter generator power a house?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A 120V model can power essentials through extension cords: a refrigerator, freezer, furnace blower, lights and internet fit under 3,500 propane watts if the motors start one at a time. Running household circuits through the panel needs a 120/240V unit like the Champion 201417 or Westinghouse iGen12000TFc, plus an electrician-installed inlet and transfer switch or interlock."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a dual fuel inverter run an RV air conditioner on propane?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Usually, in the 3,500-watt class. A 13,500 BTU rooftop unit typically needs around 3,000 watts to start without a soft starter, which the Champion 201319, Generac iQ5200DF and Westinghouse iGen5000DF cover on propane. The 2,600-watt WEN DF360iX is a soft-starter case, and the 1,665-watt Champion 201183 is for RVs with no air conditioning load."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a tri fuel inverter generator worth it?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Only if your house has natural gas service and you will pay a plumber to install a proper connection. The Westinghouse iGen12000TFc then runs at up to 7,200 running watts on natural gas with no refueling. Without a gas line the third fuel adds nothing; the dual fuel Champion 201417 does the same job."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "All Metal Brake" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Power & Generators",
    tags: [
      "best dual fuel inverter generator",
      "dual fuel inverter generator",
      "propane inverter generator",
      "tri fuel inverter generator",
      "inverter generator propane run time"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <header data-hero class="bg-[#F4F6F8] border-b border-gray-200">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-10 pb-8 lg:pt-14 lg:pb-10">
        <p class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest m-0 mb-4">
          <span class="text-[#D93A00]">Buyer's Guide</span>
          <span class="text-gray-300" aria-hidden="true">&bull;</span>
          <span class="text-gray-500">Updated {dates.display}</span>
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-[2.1rem] leading-[1.15] sm:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight text-gray-900 m-0">
          Best Dual Fuel Inverter Generator
        </h1>
        <QuickAnswer products={PRODUCTS} />
        <p class="text-lg lg:text-xl text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-5 mb-0">
          Seven inverter generators that also run on propane, compared on what they make on propane, how long a 20 lb tank lasts and how loud they are rated.
        </p>
        <!-- Author & Meta -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-7">
          <AuthorAvatar size={40} />
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 m-0">Written by <a href="/authors/alex-rivers/" class="font-bold text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Alex Rivers</a></p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 m-0">Home Improvement Editor &middot; Updated {dates.display}</p>
          </div>
          <SocialProof users="" />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mt-6">
          <TrustBadge />
          <span class="flex-1 h-px bg-gray-300"></span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-3 mb-0">
          Based on manufacturer spec sheets, owner's manuals and owner reports for gasoline and propane ratings, run time, noise and outlets; we did not run these generators ourselves. No paid placements. <a href="/how-we-test/" class="font-bold text-gray-900 underline">Read how we pick</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

